\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. My soul, there is a country
\par Afar beyond the stars,
\par Where stands a winged sentry
\par All skilful in the wars.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. There, above noise, and danger,
\par Sweet peace sits, crowned with smiles,
\par And One born in a manger
\par Commands the beauteous files.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He is thy gracious friend,
\par And- O my soul, awake!
\par Did in pure love descend,
\par To die here for thy sake.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. If thou canst get but thither.
\par There grows the flower of peace,
\par The rose that cannot wither,
\par Thy fortress, and thy ease.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Leave then thy foolish ranges;
\par For none can thee secure,
\par But One, who never changes,
\par Thy God, thy Life, thy Cure.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

